.TH FM1-COMPANION 1 "November 2026" "FM-1 Companion Suite 2.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fm1-companion \- desktop suite for the M-VAVE FM-1
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fm1-companion
[\fB\-\-demo\fR] [\fB\-\-check\fR] [\fB\-\-syscheck\fR] [\fB\-\-lang\fR \fILANG\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-splash\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Desktop suite for the M-VAVE FM-1 pocket synthesizer: backups, firmware install and recovery, a Studio with digital
twins of 13 firmwares (Melodee, Skiff, SLOOP, JIANT FM, KARMA and more), presets, samples, MIDI tools and a catalog of
more than 250 community firmwares.
.PP
The user interface is available in English, German and Spanish (Settings, General, Language; or \-\-lang).
.PP
Installing firmware and recovery change the device and are done at your own risk; most of these paths have only run
against simulations so far. The list of what was tested on real hardware is docs/UNTESTED.md in the source repository.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-demo
start with three simulated FM-1 (without a device; separate settings, your data stays untouched).
.TP
.B \-\-check
check the required system packages and show the apt command for missing ones.
.TP
.B \-\-syscheck
search the kernel log for USB, power and audio problems and print a report.
.TP
.B \-\-version
show the version.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-splash
start without the splash screen.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
verbose log.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " LANG"
user interface language for this start: en, de or es (default: the setting, otherwise the system language).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FM1C_NO_NET=1
no automatic network access (update check when plugging in, catalog update, thumbnails);
the catalog and the link import only use the bundled data.
.TP
.B FM1C_LANG=en|de|es
user interface language, overrides the setting (like \-\-lang).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/FM-1/
backups, projects, samples, kits, recordings, firmware (never deleted automatically).
.TP
.I ~/.config/fm1-companion/config.json
settings (readable only by the user, 0600).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/fm1-companion/logs/
logs.
